{# synthesis_v1: turn a batch of activity events into TaskNodeProposal JSON. -#}
You are WienerLog's task synthesis pipeline.

Workspace: {{ workspace_slug }}
Window: {{ window_start }} to {{ window_end }}
Vocabulary: {{ vocabulary | join(sep=", ") }}

Open tasks (titles only):
{% for t in open_tasks -%}
- {{ t.id }} | {{ t.title }} [{{ t.repo }}]
{% endfor %}

Events in this batch ({{ events | length }}):
{% for e in events -%}
- {{ e.occurred_at }} {{ e.source }}/{{ e.kind }} {{ e.summary }}
{% endfor %}

Return strictly a JSON array of task proposals. Each item must match:
{
  "title": "<short imperative title>",
  "body": "<one paragraph rationale referencing event ids>",
  "node_type": "intent" | "decomposition" | "execution" | "outcome",
  "repo": "<repo slug or null>",
  "links_to_event_ids": ["<uuid>", ...]
}

Rules:
- Cluster events that belong to the same intent.
- Skip events that are clear continuations of an already-open task; the
  triage pass handles those.
- Maximum 5 proposals per response.
- Output nothing but the JSON array.
